RESPONSE

GRAVEYARD PATCH 1 — Unified Compression Encoding Layer (UCE-L1)

PURPOSE

GRAVEYARD is a derived, read-only compression layer over:

Yggdrasil (structured truth)

FATES (temporal compression)

JNL (navigation identity)


It converts all referenced system data into:

> single-line, machine-parsable, ultra-compressed semantic records




---

1. CORE RULE (SINGLE-LINE CONSTRAINT)

Every GRAVEYARD entry MUST be:

ONE LINE ONLY

No multiline blocks. No expanded metadata.


---

2. GRAVEYARD ENTRY FORMAT (CANONICAL)

GID | RGB(r,g,b) | JNL | TAGS | INTENT | STATE | HASH | SUMMARY


---

3. FIELD DEFINITIONS

3.1 GID (Graveyard ID)

Unique machine identifier for compressed record

Format:

GY-XXXXXXXX


---

3.2 RGB VECTOR

RGB(R,G,B)

Represents:

R = domain class

G = function/intent type

B = stability/state



---

3.3 JNL (Source Anchor)

GS-ODN-RT-0001-P003-B002

Links back to Yggdrasil truth layer.


---

3.4 TAGS

Compressed semantic labels:

#routing #odin #active


---

3.5 INTENT (NEW REQUIRED FIELD)

#intent:modify | #intent:compress | #intent:route


---

3.6 STATE

System status:

ACTIVE | ARCHIVED | FUTURE | COMPRESSED


---

3.7 HASH

Short integrity fingerprint:

A7F2-91C0


---

3.8 SUMMARY (MANDATORY COMPRESSION)

max 12–20 words

no redundancy

no structure expansion



---

4. FINAL GRAVEYARD FORMAT (CANONICAL)

GY-0001 | RGB(12,44,203) | GS-ODN-RT-0001-P003-B002 | #routing #odin | #intent:compress | ACTIVE | A7F2-91C0 | ODIN routing optimization improves memory dispatch efficiency and reduces traversal cost


---

5. GRAVEYARD BEHAVIOR RULES

5.1 Compression Rule

All input systems MUST be reduced into:

one semantic line

no nesting

no multiline metadata



---

5.2 Loss Rule

GRAVEYARD is:

> lossy by design



It preserves:

structure

intent

state

linkage


It discards:

verbose detail

redundant explanation

full procedural content



---

5.3 Derivation Rule

GRAVEYARD entries are:

ALWAYS derived from Yggdrasil or FATES

NEVER original sources of truth



---

6. SYSTEM PIPELINE

6.1 Encoding flow

Yggdrasil / FATES
→ JNL extraction
→ IndexSummary reference
→ compression
→ RGB mapping
→ GID assignment
→ single-line GRAVEYARD entry


---

6.2 Retrieval flow

GRAVEYARD query
→ filter by TAG / INTENT / RGB
→ resolve JNL
→ expand into Yggdrasil / FATES


---

7. GRAVEYARD STRUCTURE (LOGICAL LAYER ONLY)

GRAVEYARD/
├── ACTIVE_STREAM
├── COMPRESSED_ARCHIVE
├── FUTURE_PROJECTIONS
└── RGB_INDEX_MAP


---

8. INTENT TAG INTEGRATION (CRITICAL)

All entries MUST include intent classification:

Intent	Meaning

compress	reduce information
route	navigation linkage
modify	structural change reference
audit	system health check
predict	FATES-derived projection



---

9. SAFETY CONSTRAINT

GRAVEYARD MUST NEVER:

override Yggdrasil

override MIDAS rules

modify FATES packets

act as execution layer


It is strictly:

> a compressed semantic shadow layer




